Session 01a1cffb-4de1-75e6-b949-1e92d45a76cf. Plan: plan/2026-11-02-push-pull-dispatch-fanout-parity.md (+ .zh-tw.md, diagrams/02-pull-dispatch-fanout.svg). Commit prefix [CEN-1637]. Toolchain: rust 1.85.0 pinned by rust-toolchain.toml; cargo/tokio 1.49.0 per Cargo.lock.

Plan files were already revised in the working tree (owner-supplied). Committed unchanged as `[CEN-1637] docs: revise pull dispatch fan-out parity plan`; the plan itself is never edited during implementation.

Phase 4.1 + 4.4 dispatcher work (`crates/rocketmq-classic-consumer/src/push/pull_service.rs`):
Decision: replace `PULL_RPC_WORKER_COUNT = 4` / `PULL_RPC_QUEUE_CAPACITY = 64` and the shared mpsc receiver with an owned `tokio::task::JoinSet<()>`. `PullRpcWorkerSet` now stores `Weak<PushConsumer>`, `Arc<PullScheduler>`, the watch sender, the JoinSet and a separate `Arc<AtomicUsize>` active counter; `None` means admission is closed. Chose JoinSet over a `HashMap<PullIdentity, JoinHandle>` because a self-removing handle map can detach an unfinished task's tail and misses abort-before-first-poll cleanup.
Decision: `PullCompletionGuard` (request + scheduler + active counter) is constructed before `JoinSet::spawn` and moved into the future, so completion, failed `Weak` upgrade, panic unwinding, watch cancellation and abort-before-first-poll each release exactly one scheduler slot; the guard never touches dispatcher state and holds no strong consumer reference. The pull future is scoped inside `run_owned_pull` so it drops before the guard, and the receiver's current value is checked before the biased `select!` so a task first polled after cancellation issues no RPC.
Decision: `try_submit` keeps one lock acquisition by delegating to private generic `submit_with(owner_weak, request)`; under that lock it rejects absent state, reaps finished tasks with `JoinSet::try_join_next` (panics reported, cancellations ignored), clones the cancellation/consumer/scheduler/counter, increments the counter, builds the guard and spawns. No await and no scheduler call occurs while the dispatcher lock is held. Verified `PullService`'s owned pull worker invokes `ConsumerRuntime::pull_message` inside a Tokio task (`crates/rocketmq-classic-core/src/runtime/pull.rs`), so spawning from admission is legal; that stage's unbounded FIFO is unchanged.
Decision: `stop(wait_millis)` takes the set (atomically closing admission), signals cancellation, joins with `join_next` under one deadline, then `abort_all` and drains all join results so guards run. `Drop` signals cancellation and lets the owned JoinSet abort; cleanup is observed when the runtime polls the aborts, not synchronously in `Drop`. Test accessor `worker_count()` replaced by `active_admissions()` reading the separate counter (JoinSet::len counts completed unjoined tasks); `PullScheduler::worker_count()` unchanged.
Rust 1.85 constraint: `let`-chains are unstable on this pinned toolchain, so join-result classification uses a small `report_join` match helper instead of `if let ... && ...`.
Tests (same file, `mod tests`): replaced the fixed-set test with admission/concurrency/lifecycle coverage driven through `schedule`/`take_due` identity admission and the same guard/spawn/join path as production via private `submit_with` (no public testing API): 80 distinct queue identities admitted and proven concurrently entered on a release barrier plus retained active-counter witness; deferred follow-up released exactly once with raw scheduler `in_flight` inspected while the scheduler is still running; expired-`Weak` production path; panic and watch-cancellation join observation; abort of a polled pending task; abort before first poll (no yield between admission and zero-budget stop); dispatcher `Drop`; admission racing stop with a zero wait budget where each request is either owned-and-drained or returned to the caller; retiring-generation completion cannot release a new generation's slot; completed entries reaped across 200 rounds (`JoinSet::len` stays bounded). A test-only `Debug for PullRequest` was added so admission results can be unwrapped without changing production types.
Call-site audit (§4.3): `rg -n 'PullRpcWorkers::new|pull_rpc_workers|worker_count\(\)|BROKER_SUSPEND_MAX_TIME_MILLIS' crates/rocketmq-classic-consumer/src` shows only dispatcher-count assertions changed: `src/push/consumer/tests.rs` startup expectation now zero active admissions before any assignment, and the three shutdown assertions renamed to `active_admissions()`. Consume-service and scheduler count assertions kept. Startup/shutdown acquisition order unchanged (`PullSchedulerStarted` -> `PullRpcWorkersStarted`, rollback and shutdown keep scheduler-stop then dispatcher-stop); no signature change; POP path untouched in this phase.
Checks: `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-consumer --lib push::pull_service::tests --locked` PASS 17/17 (plus 289 filtered). `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-consumer --lib --locked` PASS 306/306. `cargo fmt --all` applied; `cargo clippy -p rocketmq-classic-consumer --all-targets --locked` clean.
